-## 1c. CONTRACT: a new keyword on `Retrying`/`AsyncRetrying`/`@retry`
+## 1b5. Wait composition (`+`, `sum()`, `wait_combine`, `wait_chain`) and the `wait=` value
+Verified in `tenacity/wait.py`, `tenacity/__init__.py`, `tenacity/asyncio/__init__.py`, git log.
+- `WaitBaseT = wait_base | Callable[[RetryCallState], float | int]` (`wait.py`): a plain
+  function is a first-class wait strategy. INVARIANT: every site that invokes a wait strategy
+  passes the retry state POSITIONALLY, as the loop does (`self.wait(retry_state)`), because a
+  user callable may name its parameter anything. List the keyword call sites with
+  `grep -n "(retry_state=retry_state)" tenacity/wait.py`: at the base commit `wait_combine`
+  and `wait_chain` (both iterate user strategies) and `wait_random_exponential`
+  (`super().__call__`, a method, harmless). Fix the ones the task names; name the others in the
+  final message.
+- Operator dispatch: `wait_base + x` always reaches `wait_base.__add__` (builds
+  `wait_combine(self, x)`). `wait_base.__radd__` is reached only for a left operand without a
+  working `__add__`: the int `0` seed of `sum()`, a plain function, or a non-zero number.
+  INVARIANT (reno `wait-radd-int-6f1a3c9d84b2e057.yaml`, commit 7c3c45c, #677): a non-zero
+  NUMBER on the left (`5 + wait_fixed(1)`, also a float such as `1.5 + ...`) returns
+  `NotImplemented`, so `TypeError` is raised at the addition, not later when the combined
+  wait is called. When `__radd__` is extended, branch on `callable(other)` for the
+  `wait_combine(other, self)` case; "not an int" is not "callable" (floats, `Decimal`,
+  `Fraction` would slip through).
+- The `wait=` value is consumed in TWO `_run_wait` methods: `BaseRetrying._run_wait`
+  (`tenacity/__init__.py`, also used by `TornadoRetrying`) and `AsyncRetrying._run_wait`
+  (`tenacity/asyncio/__init__.py`, awaits through `_utils.wrap_to_async_func(self.wait)`).
+  A change to how `wait` is interpreted goes in both. The falsy values `None`/`0`/`sum([])`
+  (which is the int `0`) mean "no wait" (`upcoming_sleep = 0.0`); commit e6ef84a (#679) removed
+  that guard in both places believing `wait` is never falsy.
+- Typing invariant: mypy runs with `strict`, `warn_unreachable`, `truthy-bool` and
+  `redundant-expr` (`pyproject.toml [tool.mypy]`). A runtime guard for a value the annotation
+  excludes is flagged as unreachable/redundant; the repo fix is to WIDEN the annotation to the
+  values that must work, not `# type: ignore`. The recent strictness commits (#677, #679, #682)
+  narrowed behaviour to the annotations; when restoring behaviour one of them removed, read
+  its message and reno note (`git show <sha>`) and keep the intent it states (as above).
+  Widening can leave an existing test's `# type: ignore[...]` unused (e.g. `wait=sum(  #
+  type: ignore[arg-type]` in `test_wait_arbitrary_sum`). Leave that existing test line as is
+  (see guardrails) and name it in the final message as a follow-up.
+- Changing the accepted type of an existing `Retrying` option (e.g. `wait`) is a §1c change:
+  the annotation appears in `BaseRetrying.__init__`, `BaseRetrying.copy()` (`| object`,
+  usually already wide enough), `AsyncRetrying.__init__`, and BOTH keyword `retry()`
+  overloads in `tenacity/__init__.py`. Check with `grep -n '"WaitBaseT' tenacity/__init__.py
+  tenacity/asyncio/__init__.py`: every hit except `copy()` must show the same widened type,
+  or `@retry(wait=None)` stays a type error for users while `Retrying(wait=None)` is accepted.
+- Async: the sync `wait_combine`/`wait_chain` call members directly, so an `async def` member
+  returns a coroutine that `sum()` cannot add; only the top-level `wait=` is awaited through
+  `wrap_to_async_func`. Don't claim async plain callables work inside `+`/`wait_combine`.
+- Tests: `tests/test_tenacity.py::TestWaitConditions` (`test_wait_combine`,
+  `test_wait_arbitrary_sum`, `test_wait_chain`); async loop behaviour in
+  `tests/test_asyncio.py::TestContextManager`. A "no wait" test must make a retry actually
+  happen (fail once) or `_run_wait` is never reached.
+
